> u8ovf(x: u8 in 250..255) = x + 10
> wrap u8ovf
wrap analysis of u8ovf:
  x + 10   (u8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 6 points, e.g. x=250
      nsw holds
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 6 points, e.g. x=250
  over all 6 points of the domain
> range u8ovf
range of u8ovf -> u8:
  4..9   (6 distinct values)
  values: 4..9
  fits in u4
  over all 6 points of the domain
> i8neg(x: i8 in -128..-1) = -x
> range i8neg
range of i8neg -> i8:
  -128..127   (128 distinct values)
  fits in i8
  over all 128 points of the domain
> wrap i8neg
wrap analysis of i8neg:
  -x   (i8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 1 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 1 points, e.g. x=-128
      exact for: -127..-1
  over all 128 points of the domain
> mix8(x: i8, y: u8) = x + y
  note: mixing i8 and u8: computed as u8
> domain mix8
domain of mix8:
  x: i8, -128..127
  y: u8, 0..255
  no conditions: total on its parameter types
  defined at 65536 of 65536 points
  over all 65536 points of the domain
> wrap mix8
wrap analysis of mix8:
  u8(x)   (u8)
      truncates at 32768 points, e.g. x=-128, y=0
  u8(x) + y   (u8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 32640 points, e.g. x=-1, y=1
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 16384 points, e.g. x=127, y=1
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 16384 points, e.g. x=-128, y=0
  over all 65536 points of the domain
> range mix8
range of mix8 -> u8:
